WEBVTT

profile-create
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:14.787
Begin with a Git-backed Profile. The app can create one from Profile settings, while the C L I can initialize the same source, show the active Profile, and run its checks.

harness-publish
00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:26.525
The Profile is editable source. Check and commit it, then Sync publishes the exact agent, tools, environment, graders, and reward policy as an immutable Harness Release.

dataset-build
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:39.087
In Training, choose the chats, files, or imports that belong in the Dataset. Review disclosure, tasks, graders, and the separate train and frozen Eval boundaries before materializing it.

manifest-pin
00:00:40.237 --> 00:00:51.599
A Harness Run Manifest binds the Harness and Dataset releases to one model revision, recipe, runtime, engine, and compute target. Launch the saved Model Run with that exact manifest.

model-configure
00:00:52.749 --> 00:01:03.066
In Lab, follow Goal, Dataset, Training Method, and Model. OpenPond resolves a compatible engine and compute target without provisioning anything until the final Run review.

infrastructure-launch
00:01:04.216 --> 00:01:17.766
OpenPond Managed prepares the training environment, resolves compatible accelerator capacity, and preserves the run's artifacts and receipts. You choose the training method and budget; OpenPond operates the infrastructure behind one stable compute option.

run-inspect
00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:28.733
Once launched, the app and C L I read the same control-plane record. Watch progress, stream logs, list artifacts, or request the full status as structured JSON.

promotion-review
00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:42.108
The result remains inspectable in Lab, but promotion stays blocked until frozen evaluation and lineage checks pass. That gate protects the exact Model artifact and compatible Harness Release.
